      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T07:48:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do the devtools live in dawn::native? dawn::native is code that implements webgpu.h on top of a GPU API but the devtools do something completely different. See [this comment thread](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-YOcsCKtTRp2yyIrA7j8ZI1lJO9BtIBnlfKFK7EKksE/edit?disco\u003dAAABnfH6UC4). Please move them in `dawn/devtools` or something like that. The WebGPU backend will then depend on the recording part, while the replay may depend on the dawn::native, but all of them are decoupled because they only rely on webgpu.h and the protobuf for communication.",
      "revId": "14a4acbf4ab004e6f7af613e08e2774b7ccf5f2a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
